extra=['The carousel request set splits into 80 horizontally visible-card requests and 32 allowed adjacent/bootstrap requests on each side, plus 56 far requests on baseline and zero on candidate. These rails start below the vertical viewport in the timed windows; this fix bounds horizontal discovery and leaves native vertical lazy scheduling in place. Approximate request-time DOM visibility is retained separately from the fixed styled initial-range classification; see analysis-correction.json.', '', f'LCP was lower in {sum(x<0 for x in deltas)} pairs, higher in {sum(x>0 for x in deltas)}, and equal in {sum(x==0 for x in deltas)}. No consistent LCP improvement is demonstrated. In particular, some normal-loopback profiles increased despite reduced image traffic. With one observation per tuple and sequential processes, these timings cannot establish a causal page-speed improvement; the direct evidence is the request-set bound and unchanged tested next-image readiness.', '', 'All shared call sites and the A–N coverage/limits are enumerated in [GATES.md](GATES.md). Screenshots were directly inspected, and no human screen-reader listening session is claimed.', '']
